/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43339/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" :answer/id #uuid "a763dde3-26bc-5597-bedc-2e4887b49df2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328/selection/e18a4ca1e21416a06996f4e4fb49519cd15fc99924d4291591f2019669983c5e" :answer/id #uuid "578ebb5d-42d4-589b-b6f3-160c20921ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{50}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" :answer/id #uuid "b0a8743c-2e77-5dac-b6af-5ac66163c949" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer/id #uuid "c34abd96-d115-5a06-9fc3-2022aac0fa11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328/selection/b0e2a2f1ecf6c738e9cd90dc83077a58507e465c8147a10ba1a75ae3f17f5a3a" :answer/id #uuid "e9f2fef2-658f-5118-a1db-a4a119a929d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f42efba-3c43-5af3-b94b-2a896d82a916" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43328/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" :answer-field/choices ["q-43328/selection/cfa59613343dcd1d266f69e78114708e270fc38593403a2183ff722c45bc8c6d" "q-43328/selection/e18a4ca1e21416a06996f4e4fb49519cd15fc99924d4291591f2019669983c5e" "q-43328/selection/04a957e6e22629a4173a3ba5fec0752e198f21a1bfd1ab3b4e1aaccd930174d3" "q-43328/selection/b8903bf0f0c79152fee06a2deb1a952caebfd91f17e1376aeed868afbb728af8" "q-43328/selection/b0e2a2f1ecf6c738e9cd90dc83077a58507e465c8147a10ba1a75ae3f17f5a3a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43328" :question/id #uuid "8c947052-4de7-5f58-b63d-f4e91e0ab22b" :question/math-academy-id "q-43328" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f2a9f5e6149b62b5724de8a46e50e7aac2976ffa2f9f841c64417ffd248fcb88.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find the measure of $∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}} & =\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 1 & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43328/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43328"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280279/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "72ba36bb-85d1-5d7e-9547-5965892086b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280279/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e9abe5e8-19c8-51cc-9b14-025c933a9cec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280279/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-280279/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280279" :question/id #uuid "4cd24f26-3da7-5768-8fda-4ef54a05927a" :question/math-academy-id "q-280279" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/866f869f43e2663c2f63a485049f84ae059e2fdcb73db0445eb355491957c66a.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2}{\\text{cm}}^{2}.$ Then,  $AC=${{field-1}} $\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=10\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={120}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 10\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{25\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =5b\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ 25\\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} & =5b\\cdot \\cancel{\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}} \\\\ 5b & =25 \\\\ b & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=5\\,\\text{ cm}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280279/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-285703/field-1/5f40b464eff18ba5044f23a85ca9e5e06b5b2b71a36092be277ee86e16a2e904" :answer/id #uuid "7f1bbc69-4932-5617-add9-177028e0de9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-285703/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "60225b26-4beb-5112-95d4-575b266647ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-285703/field-1/5f40b464eff18ba5044f23a85ca9e5e06b5b2b71a36092be277ee86e16a2e904" :answer-field/choices ["q-285703/field-1/5f40b464eff18ba5044f23a85ca9e5e06b5b2b71a36092be277ee86e16a2e904"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-285703" :question/id #uuid "10670437-a53f-54a7-827c-60721e1dcb8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-285703" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/dafaf2421aaa9be80c472b4dde7c941defb94f7f3533fda4ebb2fdcee2b60e31.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/cd9363a3cc686ae45f49c982f4b31ad75b7c7897dcf7e8af58e530dba6946e1d.png)\n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & =21\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 8\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & =28\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{43}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈19.096\\,0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & ≈16.086\\,9+19.096\\,0 \\\\  & ≈35.182\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the **nearest tenth**, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $35.2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-285703/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-285703"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" :answer/id #uuid "a578e6cc-a14c-5c8e-8d7c-ebf9b8114b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768/selection/02ddd28ecf7c540455939ca8b659cf26377dff4fb2cfce0f35f284a540feeaac" :answer/id #uuid "a864abd6-a83e-5d1d-853b-a335b7ddf3d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768/selection/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" :answer/id #uuid "5f871911-3e28-5d3c-9d47-94fd9517bb92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768/selection/ad7a3824e2b90d316aedd9968e2fdff13c67ee5110546b7a43eeb384aa267fd0" :answer/id #uuid "d5bc0b6c-dfe4-5259-b044-b8d4eb6a6ec2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "112" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768/selection/c5fad6b1da11b9b990be9e0d2fcb83dfa156d8e05ce4b7ef6802ba6bbc66674b" :answer/id #uuid "84a0784d-f201-55c9-9fd2-bc6fea33b0fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "98" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f72d213-d8b9-5973-a48f-d42b67603562" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72768/selection/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" :answer-field/choices ["q-72768/selection/8cd557fa143c2616f01a8df1d19e854fea26be776628dc106639661d1b774491" "q-72768/selection/02ddd28ecf7c540455939ca8b659cf26377dff4fb2cfce0f35f284a540feeaac" "q-72768/selection/c89a78e01f135d27857f87b29786d3bde75753fd31e9ec00c0c39b58d64c0b12" "q-72768/selection/ad7a3824e2b90d316aedd9968e2fdff13c67ee5110546b7a43eeb384aa267fd0" "q-72768/selection/c5fad6b1da11b9b990be9e0d2fcb83dfa156d8e05ce4b7ef6802ba6bbc66674b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72768" :question/id #uuid "dfbe7ab7-f239-538f-a0c2-b2c3605435c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-72768" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/36af7324fd2112d94feddc5a1a02a91d97bbc0866cb93a6ca711dd73f566305a.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/7cfcb5cdf77b4afbf25afd64e37bb33f0ab2c211e09659181bfc16db0ccd2db7.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(18)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =72\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈67.658,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 67.658 \\\\  & =135.316.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $135.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72768/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72768"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787/selection/58e83169da9bb6f100f58e208ea256e70eb4d9f099387c11ded914127e54e99d" :answer/id #uuid "27505146-5134-5a54-ba92-c0c40afea1ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "69.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787/selection/654158bd8756814b4e5116d4685a7573395c52e0c0ac2e269ca7d6115142ba00" :answer/id #uuid "f5994c2f-d174-50cc-96ab-4b312b0397c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "83.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787/selection/46d07f37384b803cd740c6df79930e0e3a3093e3b2d3ceb9397b7af75c7b7be8" :answer/id #uuid "c9621403-78d9-5d37-84ca-a887fc46ee3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "73.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787/selection/48a7fa41b725178283b25c310424397315cfae3ac5c0d72158833a7fc485e841" :answer/id #uuid "a4e9d9ae-24b5-5e1d-8b09-4ed642753ca2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "88.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787/selection/412a6f4dd9df4aa3201ebaa7177c3016a43c1097fda19c4a0fd0b056c1d21c78" :answer/id #uuid "b580489e-e94f-5cbc-b27b-3c297fe21961" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "76.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "200c4f49-c890-5824-b8eb-2e8e52a478bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-67787/selection/46d07f37384b803cd740c6df79930e0e3a3093e3b2d3ceb9397b7af75c7b7be8" :answer-field/choices ["q-67787/selection/58e83169da9bb6f100f58e208ea256e70eb4d9f099387c11ded914127e54e99d" "q-67787/selection/654158bd8756814b4e5116d4685a7573395c52e0c0ac2e269ca7d6115142ba00" "q-67787/selection/46d07f37384b803cd740c6df79930e0e3a3093e3b2d3ceb9397b7af75c7b7be8" "q-67787/selection/48a7fa41b725178283b25c310424397315cfae3ac5c0d72158833a7fc485e841" "q-67787/selection/412a6f4dd9df4aa3201ebaa7177c3016a43c1097fda19c4a0fd0b056c1d21c78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-67787" :question/id #uuid "447571ef-da3a-581f-92b7-e3d7f25719b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-67787" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/488389632139d269e24958275ee20a9e5f8582fd0966e4d935487d238a463180.png)\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $△ABD$ and $△BDC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/68f5708d49577befe9bac6a7aaf6a54fcdb30dcd344367d2c69b8924093dbb61.png)\n\n \n\nFirst we find the area for $△ABD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 14\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & =84\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{42.1}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈56.315\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $△BCD:$ \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{BDC} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & =17.5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{103.8}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.994\\,8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to four decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABD}+{A}_{BDC} \\\\  & =56.315\\,8+16.994\\,8 \\\\  & =73.310\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest tenth, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $73.3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-67787/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67787"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-285737/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "1935d4a8-305b-510b-9fb0-b54f40302e9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-285737/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "b85c281b-eb20-5c69-86bf-088cc87f6ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-285737/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc3064e5-65a9-52da-8035-e036d1cf8bd0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-285737/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer-field/choices ["q-285737/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" "q-285737/field-1/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-285737" :question/id #uuid "46b5c7ca-430e-5b3c-a8d2-98242978c6b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-285737" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/48dec69962b09e9c189de23c398db63066b6da8d62a04f1cd01fdc9f333f899f.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACB$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/d6a654d3154ba8af8fc4f7654e62c6bacfede7017322aeed21a143e2634dcd14.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACB,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACB} & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)(8)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈13.856,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACB} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 13.856 \\\\  & =27.712.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the **nearest integer**, the area of the parallelogram is $28.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-285737/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-285737"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "637d6825-dc45-557b-9a44-d8fde4cd6d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "466666bc-c2f6-516d-b952-5b01d307c035" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" :answer/id #uuid "b2f05137-8fc5-57f8-98f6-6d2dc90d096a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" :answer/id #uuid "d7732a51-13c3-5363-acc3-b3fe64d4d9a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "faafefac-9945-5856-8c2c-d790b7b3a45e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fdb0015-4dcd-587c-bd43-3b48ddf3e176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-54339/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" :answer-field/choices ["q-54339/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" "q-54339/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-54339/selection/84ba06c5ef46c5ec9648beb7e3447fc668d456369383b0c063fb4b9a83b2adb9" "q-54339/selection/2671fdc3a44bd3421ded09be4e881743067a96eb4e584e442a30f737593eae71" "q-54339/selection/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-54339" :question/id #uuid "fe1c85ee-47ba-593d-bacd-c936fe57a2d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-54339" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/f1ae263b71fa17fd648464c24b307c064c9e657c2c9f6b36faf8c9819f1fb285.png)\n\nFind, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram $ABCD.$" :question/worked-solution "The diagonal $\\overset{―}{AC}$ divides the parallelogram into two congruent triangles. Therefore, the area of the parallelogram is twice the area of $△ACD$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/a60b049aef53aef28802b084b3e445fd6253978500ca981d3b799977523cdd71.png)\n\n Computing the area of $△ACD,$ we find\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}(8)(5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & =20\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{55}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈16.383,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places. Consequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & =2{A}_{ACD} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 16.383 \\\\  & =32.766.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to the nearest integer, the area of the parallelogram is $33.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-54339/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-54339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-285769/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "86e1679f-39ee-50c8-88c5-1ea2928fa9ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-285769/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc34cd4-2273-55c8-8400-de716c618712" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-285769/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-285769/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-285769" :question/id #uuid "a0277ac5-084d-5f95-96ad-7aaf91ad51d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-285769" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946476/assets/33aff6da54b72146f89bbd580a889a4050bff89bca86ddb6b74b80f62875a470.png)\n\nThe area of $ABCD$ is $5{\\text{ km}}^{2}.$   Then, the area of $△BCD$, rounded to the **nearest integer**, is{{field-1}}${\\text{km}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $△ABD.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△ABD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot AD\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2.5\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 15\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{63}^{∘} \\\\  & =6.682… \\\\  & ≈7{\\text{ km}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.\n\nThe difference of the areas of $△ABD$ and the quadrilateral $ABCD$ gives the area of $△BCD.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△BCD} & ={A}_{△ABD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =7-5 \\\\  & =2{\\text{ km}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-285769/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-285769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72764/selection/de324d260e9eea67cab18ebaae0c48f21f34d6c4bd8307b9867783dfe83e5af4" :answer/id #uuid "e0060577-42ec-5a97-b005-2452c4097dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72764/selection/5497e0720f9dc7a3528766813aff93aacad24fd5b5bb4a476a7dcd65dea8db5a" :answer/id #uuid "f4159129-2fc8-59d3-b09a-df1f80b72530" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72764/selection/5e3ef648ad2c63c5d49a13d595fe787d85922fa432557959fb1a4448ddbe0456" :answer/id #uuid "5c9ecca0-5e66-5ce5-9c26-73ed7084cedd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72764/selection/0a62de286fe99d34c6e9005080fa0d3834258de3ced41f41e29cbdfcbd416902" :answer/id #uuid "02407f4c-bc2f-57d4-a03a-816ca5fbeb3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "19{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72764/selection/e8238c6fa5601f0db4eaa803833fe1ea4f0f30720ce6f3d33c1455fbe1c37acf" :answer/id #uuid "7707ed10-f84f-5306-9010-02fcf8332461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "34{\\text{ cm}}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72764/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "60ef8113-28b4-5f71-8864-c30d1be347e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72764/selection/0a62de286fe99d34c6e9005080fa0d3834258de3ced41f41e29cbdfcbd416902" :answer-field/choices ["q-72764/selection/de324d260e9